ey found what they  described as a happy household everybody  was getting along and they and police  took no further action a few months  later little arthur was dead now whether  more could have been done will be  subject to an independent safeguarding  review  here is stephen cullen who is the chair  of the solihull  child safeguarding partnership  this terrible tragedy has had a shocking  impact on arthur's family and across the  whole community  the tragic loss of a young boy in such  terrible circumstances is dreadful  we send our heartfelt condolences to  everybody affected  the circumstances around the death will  be now subject of independent review  the local child safeguarding practice  review  and clearly it would be inappropriate  for the partnership  to comment ahead of the findings of this  review  now tustin and hughes will be sentenced  tomorrow the judge has said um there are  some terrible details to this case much  of it was caught on cctv camera because  the couple had rigged a camera up in  their lounge where they'd made arthur  sleep on the floor downstairs on his own  and they had recorded their punishment  so the court has heard audio of him  saying that no one loved him and begging  for food and drink and so traumatized  have the jury been by what they've heard  that the judge has excluded them uh for  excuse them from jury service for the  rest of their lives now  why did this couple do this well um  they said that they'd  put in this punishment regime because of  arthur's behaviour  and  tustin had said that she simply couldn't  cope with his behavior hughes admitted  that he probably valued his partner's  love  over the welfare of his child
 

